! mcp_bootstrap_p373.strap -- MCP printed page 373: the SYSTEM COMMAND
! package (PUNID 22SCOMD), the delete test and the MULTI-CHANNEL ONLY
! REQUEST unit scan (Z MULCH .. Z QUES4, the SPL message call, Z MCP MC).
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.123, read at 400 dpi, names at 900
! dpi.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 22SCOMD  CARD ID
! WA000593  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE NUMBER 373"; the heading row's
! LOCATION field is 235221, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  48 lines; every line number prints a "*".  A "*" prints
! after the LOCATION on lines 20 and 39.  No TAIL.  Still SCOMD: same
! PUNID, card series WA, no SLC.  Contiguous from 235221.00 to
! 235254.00 (line 48, a half word; next 235254.40), then blank paper.
!   lines  1-3   K,Z DELET,12 / BZAE,Z MNERX / B,Z OWNER.
!   lines  4-5   remark cards ("-" in NAME; banner on 5).
!   lines  6-20  Z MULCH: the unit scan over the requested channel.
!   lines 10,18  remark-only cards (remark continuations).
!   lines 21-46  Z DONE, Z SET PP, Z QUS 11, Z QUES4 (SIC,ZSPLP9 /
!                BD,ZSPLPR / ,Z SPL 01 / CF,5.0 message call;
!                ,D ABEOJ / BE,D MCP / ,D COMM / VF,Z QUZ 49 / CF,5.0),
!                Z MCP MC.
!   lines 47-48  SIC,Z SCAN9 / B,Z CH SCN.
! JOIN: scratch p.372 ends with a full-word BB1 at 235220.00 (next
! 235221.00) and scratch p.374 opens at 235254.40: contiguous both
! ways.  p.374's header prints CARD ID WA000641, so WA000640 prints on
! neither page (and WA000639 prints twice here).
!
! >>> CARD SERIALS. <<<  WA000593 .. WA000639, one per line, EXCEPT
! lines 47 and 48 BOTH print WA000639 (read at 400 dpi, plain ink).
! Recorded, not explained (p.197 has the same shape).
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 3 "B,ZCWNER" = ZOWNER: open round, English OWNER (S OWNER on
!     line 15 prints the same glyph); no ZCWNER anywhere.
!   * line 19 "Z MAIN D", line 23 "Z PP CHD": D (worn stem possible);
!     C22-6728 typesets ZMAIND (10x) and ZPPCHD (3x).
!   * line 35 ",Z SPL 01": the round before 1 is open; written as the
!     DIGIT (numbered name, no typeset witness; the octal fields print
!     0 open too).  ZSPL01 occurs nowhere else -- coordinator: check
!     the page that defines 235260.00.
!   * line 9 "ZQUS11": a pen stroke crosses the first 1; C22-6728
!     typesets ZQUS11, and line 25 labels "Z QUS 11".
!   * line 42 "Z QUZ 49": Q with its tail at 900 dpi (sheet read GUZ).
!   * line 40 "BE,C MCP" = DMCP (worn D; landed DMCP SYN,32.0, binary
!     000040.00).
!   * remarks: "CN" (lines 12, 26) is ON with an open O; written ON.
!   * line 34's hex byte prints "CO" and is 00 (BD, no index; the
!     octal fields print 0 open; lesson 6).  Lines 2, 14, 16 print C0
!     and assemble C0.
!
! NEIGHBOURS (scratch pp.365-376, not landed) DEFINE most SCOMD
! externals; the stand-ins copy their dds/form (see each card).  The
! K/KF second half 044606 (length 36, byte 6) agrees with p.376's
! (AX)DD(BU,36,6) for ZDELET/ZDELTM.
!
! LINES 12 AND 26: AN INDICATOR SYSTEM SYMBOL'S DDS.  CM1111,Z ASU IN and
! CM1111,Z OP TST carry NO dds, and print 001000.36 F0 -- exactly line
! 23's explicit CM1111(BU,1).  Their defining cards (p.376 lines 17,
! 18) are SYN,$PG5 / SYN,$PG6, and C28-6129 printed p.11 gives every
! indicator-bit system symbol "mode BU, byte size 8 and a field length
! equal to the length of the particular ... bit": (BU,1,8).  Until
! 2026-11-06 strap_asm gave it none and assembled length 0.
!
! >>> SPELLING CONFLICTS FOR THE COORDINATOR. <<<
!   * ZOPTST: line 26 prints "Z OP TST" (remark "SET OP CODE TEST");
!     C22-6728 typesets ZOPTST (2x).  p.376 line 18 writes "ZCPTST
!     SYN,$PG6" (remark "CP CODE TEST") -- an open O read as C there.
!   * ZSPL01: p.374 (the defining page) spells ZSPL01; p.375 writes
!     ZSPLC1 ("C vs O unsettled").  This page follows p.374.
!
! EXTERNALS.  Resident (landed): SOWNER, SUNASG, SUNITK (p.99), ZSPLP9,
! ZSPLPR (p.212), SPRIMR, SPRIME, DABEOJ, DMCP, DCOMM.  SCOMD symbols:
! forms from the scratch neighbours' defining cards, addresses checked
! against this page's binary.

SOWNER  SYN(BU,1), 0.32              ! landed p.99 line 30 -PRIORITY LEVEL
SUNASG  SYN(BU,1), 0.29              ! landed p.99 line 27 -UNIT ASSIGNMENT
SUNITK  SYN(BU,4), 0.59              ! landed p.99 line 40 -UNIT COUNT
ZSPLP9  SYN, (8)224052.0             ! landed p.212 line 12
ZSPLPR  SYN, (8)224046.40            ! landed p.212 line 5
